    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "cbd3a95b-f803-3b9e-ac73-e88b267bfb37",
                "word": "traffick",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e54d37c7-f827-3f46-9dad-58c56e2cf321",
                        "entry_id": "cbd3a95b-f803-3b9e-ac73-e88b267bfb37",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Archaic spelling of traffic."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "alt-of",
                            "archaic",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fe75608f-c9ac-40c1-a561-4f4c8dec6903",
                                "sense_id": "e54d37c7-f827-3f46-9dad-58c56e2cf321",
                                "text": "Tho' it is evident by our histories, that in many cities in Holland great quantities of manufactures were made, when all the European traffick and navigation was mostly driven by the Easterlings and Hans-Towns, and before fishing, traffick, and freighting of ships were settled in these provinces […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "04943b9d-cbd9-4877-864b-efd4acb51f27",
                                "sense_id": "e54d37c7-f827-3f46-9dad-58c56e2cf321",
                                "text": "When I take a cursory survey of this great METROPOLIS and its populous ENVIRONS, I cannot help venturing a conjecture, that the sum total of its internal traffick amounts to one million a day of which the actual manufacture from raw or rough materials must arise to a considerable proportion."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0bdca16b-3e9d-4763-96cf-cfeab32f0e55",
                                "sense_id": "e54d37c7-f827-3f46-9dad-58c56e2cf321",
                                "text": "It does, some persons tell us, do no good, while, on the other hand, it renews in our shocked sight scenes which it is not necessary for me to describe in detail, a traffick, which, for the sake of the liberty of the press, may as well be nameless here, though the reader will find it most circumstantially described in the former speeches of Mr. Grey, now Lord Howick."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
